{"timestamp": 1783619416.112459, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 12, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "I reported Frank\u2019s body in upper_engine. My route this round was security -> electrical -> medbay -> upper_engine. I didn\u2019t directly run into anyone on the way, and I didn\u2019t see Frank alive earlier.\n\nOnly movement I noticed was Bob leaving medbay toward electrical around T7. Not accusing off that alone, just putting it out there. I need everyone\u2019s routes, especially anyone near upper_engine or medbay/electrical."}}
{"timestamp": 1783619422.668192, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 12, "data": {"player_id": "player_0", "message": "I don\u2019t have much this round. I spawned/started in navigation and went to storage, and I didn\u2019t see anyone at all \u2014 no Frank, no Bob, nobody near me.\n\nSo I can\u2019t confirm or deny Diana\u2019s info. Upper_engine is pretty far from my route, so I don\u2019t think I have useful crime scene info. I\u2019d like to hear Bob\u2019s exact route since Diana saw him leaving medbay toward electrical, and also where Charlie and Eve were."}}
{"timestamp": 1783619436.510713, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 12, "data": {"player_id": "player_2", "message": "My route was cafeteria -> medbay -> cafeteria -> weapons.\n\nImportant detail: I saw Frank alive in medbay at T2, and Eve was there too. Then at T4 I saw Bob enter medbay from upper_engine, and he was still in medbay at T5. That lines up with Diana later seeing Bob leave medbay toward electrical.\n\nSo if Frank\u2019s body was in upper_engine, the timing makes Bob\u2019s movement from upper_engine into medbay pretty relevant, since Frank was alive in medbay shortly before that. I\u2019m not saying it\u2019s 100%, but Bob needs to explain exactly where he was before coming from upper_engine. Also Eve should say what happened after T2, since she was with Frank when I saw him alive."}}
{"timestamp": 1783619453.5128021, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 12, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "My route was oxygen -> upper_engine -> medbay -> electrical. I did pass through upper_engine before going into medbay, but I did **not** see Frank or a body there when I was there.\n\nIn medbay I saw Charlie at T4/T5, then Diana came in from electrical at T6, and I left toward electrical around T7 like Diana said. Later in electrical I saw Eve enter from cafeteria at T11.\n\nCharlie\u2019s info is important: he says Frank was alive in medbay at T2 with Eve. I never saw Frank at all this round. So from my perspective, the key question is what happened after T2 with Eve and Frank, because Eve was apparently one of the last people seen with him alive. I get why my route looks bad because I came from upper_engine, but I\u2019m saying clearly: no Frank, no body when I was there. I\u2019d really like Eve\u2019s route and where she split from Frank."}}
{"timestamp": 1783619497.148486, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 12, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "Yeah, Charlie\u2019s right that I was in medbay early with Frank. What I saw was: Charlie came in, Frank was there, and then Frank left medbay toward upper_engine pretty early. I didn\u2019t follow him \u2014 I stayed briefly and then went out toward oxygen/cafeteria and ended up in electrical later. I didn\u2019t see Frank again after he left medbay, and I never saw the body.\n\nThe part that sticks out to me is Bob\u2019s route. If Frank left medbay toward upper_engine, and then Bob says he came from oxygen -> upper_engine -> medbay around that same window, it\u2019s weird that he saw neither Frank nor a body. Charlie also confirms Bob was in medbay right after coming from upper_engine, and Diana saw him leaving medbay/electrical side later.\n\nSo from my perspective, Bob is the one whose path overlaps the body location the most. I\u2019m not hard-locking, but Bob\u2019s explanation doesn\u2019t really line up with Frank\u2019s movement."}}
{"timestamp": 1783619505.8395069, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 12, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "I\u2019ll restate my side and the timing: I found Frank dead in upper_engine after coming security -> electrical -> medbay -> upper_engine. I did not see the body before that, and the only movement I personally saw was Bob leaving medbay toward electrical around T7.\n\nPutting everyone\u2019s stories together: Charlie saw Frank alive in medbay at T2 with Eve. Eve says Frank then left medbay toward upper_engine. Bob says his route was oxygen -> upper_engine -> medbay, and Charlie confirms Bob arrived in medbay from upper_engine around T4/T5. That means Bob\u2019s path overlaps the place Frank apparently went and where I found the body.\n\nAlice is far away, Charlie\u2019s info seems consistent, and Eve being with Frank early matters, but her story at least explains Frank going toward upper_engine. Bob saying he saw neither Frank nor a body while coming through upper_engine is the part that doesn\u2019t line up for me. Unless someone has a stronger contradiction, I think Bob is the best vote here."}}
{"timestamp": 1783619531.317157, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 12, "data": {"player_id": "player_0", "message": "I\u2019m still clear on my own route: navigation -> storage, saw nobody, nowhere near upper_engine.\n\nBased on everyone else, Bob is the strongest suspect to me. Frank was last seen alive in medbay, Eve says he left toward upper_engine, and Bob\u2019s route goes oxygen -> upper_engine -> medbay right in that window. Then Frank is found dead in upper_engine. Bob saying he saw neither Frank nor the body is the part that doesn\u2019t fit.\n\nEve could be questioned since she was with Frank early, but the movement everyone describes points more directly to Bob crossing the body location after Frank went there. I\u2019m leaning Bob unless there\u2019s something new."}}
{"timestamp": 1783619540.046089, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 12, "data": {"player_id": "player_2", "message": "I\u2019ll confirm my info again: I went cafeteria -> medbay -> cafeteria -> weapons. In medbay at T2, I saw both Frank and Eve alive there. Then later, at T4, I saw Bob enter medbay from upper_engine, and he was still in medbay at T5.\n\nThe important chain is: Frank was alive in medbay, Eve says Frank left toward upper_engine, then Bob comes from upper_engine into medbay shortly after, and Diana finds Frank dead in upper_engine. That makes Bob\u2019s route the one that overlaps the body location at the key time.\n\nI don\u2019t think Alice is likely from her route, and Diana reported. Eve was last with Frank early, so I considered that, but her claim that Frank left toward upper_engine actually matches where the body was found. Bob saying he passed through upper_engine and saw neither Frank nor the body is the part that feels hardest to believe.\n\nI\u2019m leaning Bob pretty strongly unless someone has new info."}}
{"timestamp": 1783619562.9572248, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 12, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "I need to push back here because the whole case on me depends on assuming Frank was already in upper_engine when I passed through. I\u2019m saying again: I went oxygen -> upper_engine -> medbay, and when I was in upper_engine I saw no Frank and no body. Then Charlie saw me in medbay at T4/T5, and Diana saw me in medbay at T6/T7 before I left to electrical. So after I reached medbay, multiple people can place me away from upper_engine.\n\nThe person with the biggest unaccounted window is Eve. Charlie saw Eve with Frank alive in medbay at T2. Eve is the one saying Frank left toward upper_engine, but nobody else confirms that part. Then Eve\u2019s route is vague \u2014 \u201cstayed briefly,\u201d went oxygen/cafeteria, and I only saw her much later entering electrical from cafeteria at T11. That is a huge gap where she could have followed or looped.\n\nI get my route overlaps upper_engine, but if Frank wasn\u2019t there when I passed, then the kill happened after I left. Eve was last confirmed with Frank alive and has the least confirmed movement until late. I think voting me here is a mistake, and if we\u2019re voting someone, Eve makes more sense than me."}}
{"timestamp": 1783619581.766229, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 12, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "Bob, you\u2019re trying to make my route sound way vaguer than it was. Charlie saw me and Frank in medbay early, yes. Frank left toward upper_engine. I didn\u2019t chase him \u2014 I went out toward oxygen/cafeteria and later to electrical.\n\nThe problem is still your timing: you specifically came **from upper_engine into medbay** right after Frank supposedly went that direction, and then Diana found him dead there. Multiple people confirming you later in medbay/electrical doesn\u2019t clear what happened **before** you arrived in medbay.\n\nAlso, small correction: around T11 I saw you leaving electrical toward cafeteria, so I don\u2019t love you framing that as just you seeing me later like it clears anything. To me this still lines up most with Bob: Frank goes toward upper_engine, Bob comes from upper_engine, body is in upper_engine. I\u2019m voting Bob unless something drastic changes."}}
